# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Appwrite connection.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two required values from the
# Appwrite console (Project → Overview).
#
# Both are required. Without them the app renders a "Backend not configured"
# screen instead of starting — there is no offline mode.
#
# The project id is meant to be public; it ships in the browser bundle. What
# protects your data is the table permissions created by appwrite/setup.mjs.
# Never put an API key here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Cloud endpoints look like https://<region>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1
# A self-hosted instance is https://appwrite.example.com/v1
VITE_APPWRITE_ENDPOINT=
VITE_APPWRITE_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional — only set these if you changed the ids in appwrite/setup.mjs.
# VITE_APPWRITE_DATABASE_ID=cpsm
# VITE_APPWRITE_FUNCTION_ID=admin-users

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only. Used by the scripts in appwrite/ (setup, bootstrap, seed),
# never by the browser — Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_.
# Create the key under Project → Overview → Integrations → API keys with the
# Auth, Databases and Functions scopes.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APPWRITE_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free-plan keepalive (see the README). Set both of these in the Vercel project
# settings, not just here — the daily cron that stops Appwrite pausing the
# project reads them at runtime. The route refuses to run without CRON_SECRET,
# which is what keeps it from being a public button that writes schema.
# Any long random string will do; Vercel sends it back as the bearer token.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRON_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase. The migration target — see supabase/migrations/ and the runbook.
#
# The URL and the publishable key are meant to be public and ship in the browser
# bundle; row-level security is what protects the data, not the secrecy of these.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Which backend the app talks to: "appwrite" (default) or "supabase". Temporary,
# for the length of the migration — it is what makes the cutover, and the way
# back from it, a single environment variable.
# VITE_BACKEND=appwrite

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only, and never prefixed VITE_ — Vite inlines every VITE_ variable
# into the browser bundle, and this key bypasses every row-level security policy
# in supabase/migrations/0002_rls.sql. It belongs in .env.local for the migration
# scripts and in the Vercel environment for api/, nowhere else.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
